From 80f54efd4e386eba4c454f91a4f507ccc2566e15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:09:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sim): excuse a through hole's exit face in ThreadBore

On a through hole, thread milling extends one pitch past floor_z so the
teeth cut a full thread out the bottom exit. ThreadBore previously knew
only the entry height (`top`), so bottom-face facets on the minor rim
failed `wall_radius` and convicted the lead-in and helix moves with
Gouge ("cuts past the finish surface").

Add `exit: Option<f64>` to `ThreadBore` (set from `h.through.then_some(h.floor_z)`
in `thread_rims::thread_bores`) and excuse exit-face triangles whose
vertices stay at or below `exit + WALL_BAND` and whose minor-circle
vertices stand at or above `exit - WALL_BAND`. Blind floors, intermediate
shelves, lower parts below the exit, inner steps, and cuts past the
major circle still convict.

Pinned by thread_mill_rim::a_detected_through_hole_with_tm0600_verifies_clean_and_posts,
thread_mill_rim::a_through_hole_into_a_lower_part_still_convicts,
verify::thread_bore::tests::a_through_hole_exit_face_is_excused_while_blind_and_shelves_are_not,
and operation::thread_op::tests::the_thread_grant_reads_the_threads_own_pitch_and_only_over_a_round_wall.

Fixes #2655
